WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:02.070
- [Narrator] Evergrande is the world's

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:03.880
most indebted real estate firm,

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:05.910
and it's been flooding
its social media accounts

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:07.730
with videos like this,

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:09.600
showing that the company is back to work.

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.360
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.440
- [Narrator] Meanwhile, buyers
and real estate vloggers

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:16.460
are also taking to social media

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:18.460
to complain about construction delays

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:20.710
or that they haven't
received their new homes.

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:22.800
The Wall Street Journal
examined these posts

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.960
to understand why people are upset,

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.380
even as Evergrande has been
trying to fulfill pledges

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:29.690
it has made to regulators to deliver more

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:32.070
than one million pre-sold homes.

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:34.160
If the company can't
meet it's obligations,

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:36.130
consumer confidence could tank,

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:38.040
rippling through the Chinese economy

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:40.500
and potentially impacting
the global economy.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.370
- It has definitely turned

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:46.150
from being that
prestigious developer giant

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:48.810
into something that
everyone's concerned about.

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:50.610
- [Narrator] So we
compared social media posts

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:53.200
from people waiting for homes
they've already paid for.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.100
And ones from Evergrande as it promises

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:57.880
to do whatever it takes to deliver them.

00:00:57.880 --> 00:00:59.220
But first, here's how one

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:01.690
of China's largest property
developers ended up

00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:04.000
with so many stalled construction sites.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.530
Pandemic lockdowns had
hurt the company's sales

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:08.150
and new government rules kept it

00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:09.900
from borrowing more money.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:10.990
Then this past summer,

00:01:10.990 --> 00:01:13.950
Evergrande said it was
experiencing a cash crunch

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:17.200
and construction at
many of its 778 projects

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:20.400
in 233 cities were halted.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.540
All across China, the company has offices

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:25.630
and many have their own social
media accounts on WeChat,

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:28.290
one of the country's most
popular messaging apps.

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:30.520
We looked at content
published by 20 of them

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:32.600
between September and November.

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:35.080
Most of the posts follow
a similar pattern.

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:37.030
First, the company says it's working hard

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:39.223
to deliver homes and resume construction.

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:42.860
Then there are either videos or photos

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:45.629
of workers returning
to empty project sites.

00:01:45.629 --> 00:01:47.340
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:48.810
- [Narrator] And testimonials from buyers

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:51.934
who've signed contracts to
move into their new homes.

00:01:51.934 --> 00:01:54.510
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:55.343
- [Narrator] These homeowners

00:01:55.343 --> 00:01:56.950
are among the many urban Chinese

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:59.300
who plowed their savings into new homes.

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:02.570
Collectively, they have nearly
78% of their wealth tied up

00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:03.920
in residential property.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:05.830
- The property market in China

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:08.990
is very important to its economy.

00:02:08.990 --> 00:02:10.710
Real estate activity accounts

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:14.590
for roughly 1/4 of China's
GDP and a central concern

00:02:14.590 --> 00:02:16.220
for the government is making sure

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:19.250
that people get the
properties that they paid for.

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:20.790
- [Narrator] Economists
and real estate agents

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:22.840
in China say there's a lot at stake.

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:24.630
Evergrande has an estimated

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:27.830
1.4 million pre-sold
apartments outstanding.

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:28.900
And if they aren't finished,

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:31.380
many households could
suffer painful losses,

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:34.130
shaking confidence in the
country's property market.

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:36.530
And a downturn in the world's
second-largest economy

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:38.140
could spread to other countries trying

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:40.070
to bounce back from the pandemic.

00:02:40.070 --> 00:02:43.030
- So Evergrande has to make
this their priority as well,

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:45.110
and the best way to deliver the flats

00:02:45.110 --> 00:02:47.700
is to find ways to resume construction.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:48.533
- [Narrator] Local authorities

00:02:48.533 --> 00:02:50.120
are also helping out the company.

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:52.110
Most of the cities with
Evergrande projects

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:54.980
have set up task forces
to help manage the process

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:57.900
and hired accountants to
comb through their finances.

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:00.070
In early November,
Evergrande said it had handed

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:03.960
over more than 57,000 homes
between July and October.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:06.510
- These announcements
can give a bit of hope

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:08.920
to buyers who are in a desperate situation

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:10.560
of having poured so much money

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:13.220
into these unfinished
apartments they've bought.

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:15.420
And this is probably just the beginning

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:17.510
of this colossal process

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:21.440
to restart constructions
at these unfinished sites,

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:24.910
and many, many more are still
waiting for their homes.

00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:25.910
- [Narrator] And some of those waiting

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:28.230
have been using various
social media platforms

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:30.050
to vent their frustration.

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:31.790
We looked at 20 posts from buyers

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:34.110
who said that construction
appeared stalled

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:36.880
or doubted they would move into
their new homes on schedule.

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:37.940
- I do want to point out

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:42.310
that some buyers have expressed
relief on social media

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:43.990
about finally getting their homes

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:47.270
and that others also have
complained about water

00:03:47.270 --> 00:03:51.370
and gas leaks, or even
unfinished interiors.

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:54.500
And people have seen
empty construction sites,

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:58.490
so how the company is gonna turn around

00:03:58.490 --> 00:04:00.750
will be scrutinized by people

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:03.420
because this involves
something as intimate

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:05.950
and as important to them as their homes.

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:07.730
- [Narrator] Evergrande
has promised home buyers

00:04:07.730 --> 00:04:09.620
to deliver what they have paid for

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:11.420
but there are also unfinished buildings

00:04:11.420 --> 00:04:13.590
with apartments that haven't been sold

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:15.690
and a lower priority for the company.

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:17.580
We looked at posts from
real estate vloggers

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:18.930
who review property sites

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:20.470
and provide investment tips,

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:22.270
and they've been doing
their own inspections

00:04:22.270 --> 00:04:23.902
of Evergrande projects.

00:04:23.902 --> 00:04:28.240
(speaking in foreign language)

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:29.180
- [Narrator] This footage was filmed

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:31.350
by real estate vlogger He Peiqi.

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:33.340
She went to this site
called Evergrande City

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:36.000
in Hhhot, Inner Mongolia in November.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.040
A month earlier, the company posted photos

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:39.165
of Evergrande City,

00:04:39.165 --> 00:04:42.520
and said more than 1,400
apartments across six buildings

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:43.359
have been finished.

00:04:43.359 --> 00:04:47.276
(speaking in foreign language)

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:49.870
- [Narrator] This footage shows

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:51.707
that about a month
after that announcement,

00:04:51.707 --> 00:04:54.050
Evergrande City had
other buildings waiting

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:56.130
to resume construction.

00:04:56.130 --> 00:04:58.010
Evergrande says it's
working with the government

00:04:58.010 --> 00:05:00.510
and in early December, the
government of Guangdong,

00:05:00.510 --> 00:05:02.430
the province where the company is based,

00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:03.890
said it will send a working group

00:05:03.890 --> 00:05:05.990
to help the developer
work out its problems

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:08.190
and maintain normal operations.

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:10.450
Evergrande has around $20 billion worth

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:12.080
of outstanding dollar bonds

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:14.110
and it's managed to
avoid defaulting on them

00:05:14.110 --> 00:05:17.250
by making last-minute
interest payments on deadline.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:18.860
For this video, the company declined

00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:20.430
to respond to requests for comment

00:05:20.430 --> 00:05:23.140
on specific instances
of delayed construction,

00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:25.420
the poor quality of some finished homes

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:26.730
and whether the company was aware

00:05:26.730 --> 00:05:28.640
of complaints on social media.

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:30.360
So until the home owners get the keys

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:31.900
to the apartments they bought,

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:34.720
they have social media to share
their concerns with others

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:36.849
and check on the progress of their homes.

00:05:36.849 --> 00:05:39.516
(pensive music)

